course: dictionary
lesson: 9000
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «She made a quick sketch of the horse.» Here a sketch is a drawing. «The comedy show had a funny sketch about a lost dog.» Here a sketch is a short, funny scene.
explain: Sketch can also be an action, a verb. «Can you sketch out a plan for our trip?» Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or something someone does? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sketchy is slang, mostly used in America. «That website looked sketchy, so I closed it.» Sketchy means dodgy or not trustworthy. Slang words are not always in every dictionary, so the clues around them matter most.
fact: Sketch can be a noun (a sketch, sketches) or a verb (sketch, sketched, sketching).
fact: «Sketch» means a quick drawing that shows the main shapes without much detail.
fact: «Sketch» can also mean a short, funny scene in a comedy show or school play.
fact: «Sketchy» is slang, mostly American, and means dodgy, unsafe or suspicious.
fact: Useful phrases are a rough sketch, sketch out a plan, and sketchbook.
exercise: «The artists lightly sketch big simple shapes first, then add details.» What does sketch mean here? | To paint with thick colours | *To draw quickly, showing the main shapes | To cut a shape out of card | To shout the name of a shape
exercise: «The school play had a funny sketch about a lost dog.» What is a sketch here? | A picture of a dog's tail | A map of the school grounds | A song with no words | *A short, funny scene in a play
exercise: «Mia wanted to sketch out a plan for the summer.» What does sketch out mean? | Hide a plan under the bed | Tear up a plan into small pieces | *Describe a plan with only the main points | Paint a plan in bright colours
test: «That website looked sketchy, so I closed it.» What does sketchy mean? | *Dodgy or not trustworthy | Brightly coloured | Full of drawings | Very fast
test: Which phrase from the lesson means a first, rough version of a drawing or plan? | Sketchbook | Comedy show | *A rough sketch | Sketchy website
exam: «I made a sketch, then I sketched the tree.» Which word is a verb? | a sketch | tree | I | *sketched
